.zig, sacred.zig, computational.zig, non_euclidean.zig, format.zig, commands.zig\n\nReport the file paths, function signatures, and whether tests already exist.","agentId":"a201586","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive view of the geometry module. Let me compile the final report.\n\n## Geometry Module Analysis Report\n\nBased on my thorough examination of the geometry module in `src/tri/geometry/`, here's a complete summary of pure math functions and existing tests:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **mod.zig** — Core Constants & Types\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/mod.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- `pub fn orientation(p: Point2D, q: Point2D, r: Point2D) i8` — Ternary orientation test (CCW/collinear/CW)\n- `pub fn hausdorffDimension(copies: f64, scale_factor: f64) f64` — Fractal dimension calculator\n- `PlatonicSolid.surfaceArea(a: f64) f64` — Surface area for edge length a\n- `PlatonicSolid.volume(a: f64) f64` — Volume for edge length a\n- `PlatonicSolid.circumradius(a: f64) f64` — Circumradius calculation\n- `PlatonicSolid.inradius(a: f64) f64` — Inradius calculation\n- `PlatonicSolid.dihedralAngleDeg() f64` — Dihedral angle (precomputed)\n- `PlatonicSolid.eulerCheck() bool` — V - E + F = 2 verification\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 8 tests\n- `test \"euler formula for all platonic solids\"`\n- `test \"sierpinski dimension equals bits per trit\"`\n- `test \"trinity identity phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3\"`\n- `test \"orientation returns ternary values\"`\n- `test \"hausdorff dimension known values\"`\n- `test \"unit cube volume and surface area\"`\n- `test \"unit tetrahedron volume\"`\n\n---\n\n### 2. **platonic.zig** — Platonic Solids\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/platonic.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- `fn findSolid(name: []const u8) ?mod.PlatonicSolid` — Solid lookup by name\n- All math computed via `PlatonicSolid` methods (from mod.zig)\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 2 tests\n- `test \"findSolid matches prefix\"`\n- `test \"all solids have euler = 2\"`\n\n---\n\n### 3. **fractal.zig** — Fractal Geometry\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/fractal.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- `pub fn convexHull(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, points: []const mod.Point2D) ![]mod.Point2D` — Graham scan algorithm (wraps in allocator, but core algorithm is pure)\n- `fn pow3(exp: u32) u64` — 3^exp calculation\n- `fn pow3_u32(exp: u32) u32` — 3^exp (u32 version)\n- `fn isCantorPoint(pos: u32, level: u32, segment_size: u32) bool` — Cantor set membership test\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 4 tests\n- `test \"sierpinski dimension\"`\n- `test \"koch dimension\"`\n- `test \"cantor dimension\"`\n- `test \"pow3\"`\n\n---\n\n### 4. **computational.zig** — Computational Geometry\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/computational.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- `pub fn convexHull(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, points: []const mod.Point2D) ![]mod.Point2D` — Graham scan convex hull (uses allocator for stack, algorithm is pure)\n- `pub fn pointInPolygon(point: mod.Point2D, polygon: []const mod.Point2D) i8` — Ray casting point-in-polygon (returns ternary: +1/0/-1)\n- `fn parsePoint(s: []const u8) ?mod.Point2D` — Parse \"x,y\" format (not pure math, but utility)\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 5 tests\n- `test \"parsePoint valid\"`\n- `test \"parsePoint invalid\"`\n- `test \"point in unit square\"`\n- `test \"convex hull of triangle returns triangle\"`\n- `test \"trit lattice has 27 points\"`\n\n---\n\n### 5. **sacred.zig** — Sacred Geometry\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/sacred.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- Vesica Piscis: `height = r * sqrt(3)`, `area = r^2 * (2π/3 - sqrt(3))`\n- Pentagon: `diagonal = s * phi`, `area = s^2 * sqrt(25 + 10*sqrt(5)) / 4`, `apothem = s / (2*tan(π/5))`, `circumradius = s / (2*sin(π/5))`\n- Flower of Life: `C(k) = 1 + 3k(k+1)` — circle count formula\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 3 tests\n- `test \"vesica piscis height/width ratio = sqrt(3)\"`\n- `test \"pentagon diagonal/side = phi\"`\n- `test \"flower of life formula\"`\n\n---\n\n### 6. **non_euclidean.zig** — Non-Euclidean Geometry\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/non_euclidean.zig`\n\n**Pure Math Functions:**\n- `pub fn haversineDistance(lat1_deg: f64, lon1_deg: f64, lat2_deg: f64, lon2_deg: f64) f64` — Great circle distance on sphere (K > 0)\n- Spherical triangle area: `excess = A + B + C - π` (angle excess)\n- Hyperbolic triangle area: `defect = π - (A + B + C)` (angle defect)\n\n**Existing Tests:** Yes, 3 tests\n- `test \"haversine equator to pole\"`\n- `test \"haversine same point\"`\n- `test \"haversine antipodal\"`\n\n---\n\n### 7. **format.zig** — Output Formatting Utilities\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/format.zig`\n\n**Functions:** All are formatting/display utilities, NOT pure math\n- `pub fn boxHeader()`, `boxFooter()`, `sectionHeader()`, `separator()`\n- `pub fn labelFloat()`, `labelFloatUnit()`, `labelInt()`, `labelStr()`\n- `pub fn tritIndicator()`, `tritResult()` — Color-coded ternary display\n- `pub fn verified()` — Verification indicator\n\n**Tests:** None (not needed for formatting)\n\n---\n\n### 8. **commands.zig** — Command Dispatcher\n**File Path:** `/Users/playra/trinity-w1/src/tri/geometry/commands.zig`\n\n**Functions:** All are CLI command dispatchers, NOT pure math\n- `pub fn runGeometryCommand()` — Main router\n\n**Tests:** None (CLI dispatcher)\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| File | Math Functions | Tests Exist | Key Testable Functions |\n|------|----------------|-------------|----------------------|\n| mod.zig | 8 | ✓ 8 tests | orientation, hausdorffDimension, Platonic methods, eulerCheck |\n| platonic.zig | 1 (findSolid) | ✓ 2 tests | findSolid, Platonic methods (via mod) |\n| fractal.zig | 4 | ✓ 4 tests | pow3, isCantorPoint, Hausdorff dims |\n| computational.zig | 3 | ✓ 5 tests | convexHull, pointInPolygon, parsePoint |\n| sacred.zig | ~5+ formulas | ✓ 3 tests | Vesica area, Pentagon ratio, Flower formula |\n| non_euclidean.zig | 3 | ✓ 3 tests | haversineDistance, spherical/hyperbolic area |\n| format.zig | 0 pure math | ✗ 0 | Display only |\n| commands.zig | 0 pure math | ✗ 0 | CLI router |\n\n**Total Tests Existing:** 28 tests across all modules\n\n---\n\n## Key Observations\n\n1. **Ternary Math is Central**: Orientation test and point-in-polygon both return `i8` with values `{-1, 0, +1}`, making geometry inherently ternary.\n\n2. **Strong Test Coverage**: Most pure math functions already have tests, especially:\n   - Platonic solids (all 5 verified with Euler formula)\n   - Fractal dimensions (Sierpinski, Koch, Cantor)\n   - Haversine distance\n\n3. **Testable but Untested**:\n   - Individual Platonic solid volume/surface calculations (tested via Euler check, but not unit-by-unit)\n   - Vesica Piscis area calculation (only height/width tested)\n   - Pentagon apothem and circumradius (only diagonal/side tested)\n   - Flower of Life circle formula (only basic formula tested)\n   - Spherical/hyperbolic triangle areas (no direct area tests, only angle sum checks)\n\n4. **No Tests for**:\n   - Cantor set membership check detail (`isCantorPoint`)\n   - Convex hull correctness beyond simple triangle\n   - Point-in-polygon with degenerate cases"}],"totalDurationMs":30597,"totalTokens":68083,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41006,"cache_read_input_tokens":24629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":41006,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2441,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}}
